  "doctrine": [],
  "note": "Lam.5.13 leaves the load unnamed beyond its connection with grinding. The parallel burden of wood supports a millstone, though grain for grinding has also been proposed. Geʿez ጥሕን (Dillmann col. 1217) and Sabaic ṭḥn name the product, flour. Kogan, Proto-Semitic Lexicon §9.6.1, also records the grinding verb in Mehri, Jibbali and Soqotri and an early spelling in the Ebla vocabulary, VE 656. The index groups the Hebrew words with טחח, whose plastering forms belong to טוח."
